hadiths[24]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1524","# Translation of the Hadith

**Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd al-Muharibi al-Kufi narrated to us, saying:** Sharik narrated to us, from Abu al-Hasna', from al-Hakam, from Hanish, from 'Ali رضي الله عنه, that he used to offer two rams as a sacrifice (udhiyah): one on behalf of the Prophet ﷺ and the other on behalf of himself. When he was asked about this, he said: **""He commanded me to do so""** — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — **""and I shall never abandon it.""**

Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: **""This is a gharib (uncommon) Hadith. We do not know it except through the narration of Sharik.""**

He further stated: **""Some of the people of knowledge have permitted that a sacrifice be offered on behalf of the deceased, while others have held that no sacrifice should be offered on their behalf.""**

'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak said: **""It is more beloved to me that charity be given on behalf of the deceased rather than a sacrifice be offered for them. However, if one does sacrifice, they should not eat anything from it and should give all of it in charity.""**

Muhammad (al-Bukhari) said: 'Ali ibn al-Madini said: **""This Hadith has also been narrated by narrators other than Sharik.""**

I asked him: **""What is the name of Abu al-Hasna'?""** He did not know it. Muslim said: **""His name is al-Hasan.""**

---

*This narration is recorded in Sunan al-Tirmidhi and pertains to the permissibility of offering a sacrificial animal on behalf of the Prophet ﷺ after his passing, a matter upon which the scholars have differed.*"
"1525","""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered a horned male ram of fine pedigree, (around) his mouth was black, and his legs were black, and (around) his eyes was black."
"1526","Narrated by al-Bara' ibn 'Azib (may Allah be pleased with him), who reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

""One should not sacrifice a lame animal whose lameness is apparent, nor a one-eyed animal whose blindness is obvious, nor a sick animal whose illness is evident, nor an emaciated animal that has no marrow in its bones."""
"1527","he should be given a name, and his head should be shaved."
"1528","""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered that we check the eyes and ears, and not to slaughter the Muqabalah, nor the Mudabarah, nor the Sharqa', nor the Kharqa'"""
"1529","""The Muqabalah is the one whose ears have been severed, the Mudabarah is the one with the sides of its ears cut off, and the Sharqa' is one with its ears split, and the Khurqa' is the one whose ears have a hole pierced through them."""
"1530","""I brought a Jadha' sheep to Al-Madinah (for sale) but it remained with me. I saw Abu Hurairah and I asked him about it, so he said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: ""The best male"" - or - ""female Udhiyah is that from the Jadha' sheep."" He said: ""So the people took note of that (they became interested in buying)."""
"1531","That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) gave him sheep to distribute among his Companions as a sacrifice. ""There remained a young male kid or a young billy goat, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and he said: 'Sacrifice it for yourself.'""
Waki' said: ""The Jadha' among sheep is seven or six months."""
"1532","""The Prophet (ﷺ) distributed the sacrificial animals and I was left with a Jadha', so I asked the Prophet (ﷺ) about it and he said: 'Sacrifice it for yourself.'""
(Another chain) with this Hadith."
"1533","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""O 'Abdur-Rahman! Do not ask for a position of leadership"
"1534","""We performed the Nahr (sacrifice) with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at Al-Hudaibiyyah: A camel for seven (persons) and a cow for seven (persons)."""
"1535","""Ali said: 'A cow is for seven.' I said: ""And if it gives birth?' He said: 'Then slaughter its offspring with it.' I said: 'What if it is lame?' He said: 'When it has reached the place of ritual.' I said: 'What if it has a broken horn?' He said: 'There is no harm, we were ordered' - or - 'The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered us, to check the two eyes and the two ears.'"""
"1536","""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited that an animal with a A'dab (stump) horn or ear should be slaughtered as a sacrifice."" Qatadah (one of the narrators) said: ""So I mentioned this to Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab and he said: 'The A'dab is that which equals or more than that.'"""
"1537","""I asked Abu Abyub  how the slaughtering was done during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). He said: 'A man would sacrifice a sheep for himself and the people in his household. They would eat from it and feed others, until the people (later) would boast about it and it became as you see now."""
"1538","That a man asked Ibn 'Umar about the Udhiyah, ""Is it obligatory?"" So he said: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) performed the Udhiyah as did the Muslims."" He repeated the question. So he said: ""Do you understand ?"" The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) slaughtered as did the Muslims."""
"1539","Narrated Sa'd bin 'Ubaidah:That Ibn 'Umar heard a man saying: ""No by the Ka'bah"" so Ibn 'Umar said: ""Nothing is sworn by other than Allah"
"1540","# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by al-Bara' ibn 'Azib (may Allah be pleased with him):**

He said: ""The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) addressed us on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Nahr) and said: **'None of you should slaughter until he has prayed.'**

So my maternal uncle stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this is a day in which meat is scarce (or undesirable), and I hastened my sacrifice so as to feed my family, the people of my household, or my neighbours.'

He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **'Then repeat your slaughter (i.e., offer another sacrifice).'**

He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I have a young she-goat that is still nursing, and it is better than two sheep of meat. May I slaughter it?'

He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: **'Yes, and it is the best of your two sacrifices. And no *jadha'ah* (a young animal) shall suffice for anyone after you.'**

---

**Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said:** In this chapter (bab), there are narrations from Jabir, Jundab, Anas, 'Uwaymir ibn Ashqar, Ibn 'Umar, and Abu Zayd al-Ansari (may Allah be pleased with them all).

**Abu 'Isa said:** This is a *hasan sahih* hadith.

The practice (al-'amal) according to the majority of the scholars of knowledge is that no one should offer the sacrifice (*udhiyah*) in a city until the Imam has prayed. However, a group of scholars permitted the people of the villages to slaughter once dawn (fajr) has risen, and this is the view of Ibn al-Mubarak (may Allah have mercy on him).

**Abu 'Isa said:** The scholars have unanimously agreed (*ajma'a*) that a *jadha'ah* from among goats (*al-ma'z*) does not suffice, and they stated that a *jadha'ah* suffices only from among sheep (*al-da'n*)."
"1541","That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""None of you should eat from the meat of his sacrificial animal beyond three days."""
"1542","From his father that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I used to prohibit you from (eating) the meat of Sacrifice beyond three days so that those who have the ability would give to those who do not have it. So (now) eat  as you like, feed others, and save from it."""
"1543","""I said to the Mother of the Believers: 'Did the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibit from the meat of the sacrifice?' She said: 'No, but only a few people could slaughter, so he liked that they feed those who did not slaughter. (Later) we would store a leg to eat after ten days."""
"1544","That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There is no Fara' or 'Atirah.""
The Fara' is the first of the offspring that would be born to them, so they would slaughter it.
The 'Atirah was an animal that they would slaughter during Rajab to honor the month of Rajab, since it was the first of the sacred months."
"1545","They entered upon Hafsah bint 'Abdur-Rahman to ask her about the 'Aqiqah. She informed them that 'Aishah had informed her, that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered them that for a boy, two sheep were sufficient, and for a girl one sheep."
"1546","Narrated Thabit bin Adh-Dahhak:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam while lying"
"1547","Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! My sister vowed that she would walk to the House barefoot and without Khimar (covering).' The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Verily Allah will not do anything with the misery of your sister. She should ride"
